      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add Anvil realtime voice provider",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nOpenClaw currently has hosted speech-to-speech options beside ElevenLabs and OpenAI Realtime, but not an Anvil Voice option that can relay speech through the OpenClaw Gateway into Fakoli/Anvil fast-tier local routing. This adds a bundled `anvil-voice` realtime provider that can run speech-to-speech against an Anvil Voice realtime websocket, use the `agent-consult` brain for fast local LLM interaction, and support Voice Call audio format requirements without exposing provider secrets in the browser.\n\n## Summary\n- adds a bundled manifest-only `anvil-voice` realtime voice provider option for OpenClaw\n- wires Anvil Voice for gateway-relay speech-to-speech with `agent-consult` brain routing\n- hardens realtime URL validation, bearer auth handling, audio format negotiation, silence gating, transcript dedupe, barge-in, and connect timeout behavior\n- updates Voice Call to request G.711 mu-law 8 kHz for call audio and refreshes provider docs/reference inventory\n- lets bundled extension tooling resolve manifest-only extensions from `openclaw.plugin.json`, matching existing manifest-only bundled plugins\n\n## Evidence\n- `corepack pnpm test:extension anvil-voice` -> 19 passed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-voice-call.config.ts extensions/voice-call/src/webhook/realtime-handler.test.ts` -> 19 passed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/talk.test.ts src/gateway/talk-realtime-relay.test.ts` -> 152 passed\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.tooling.config.ts test/scripts/test-extension.test.ts test/scripts/bundled-plugin-build-entries.test.ts` -> 59 passed, 2 skipped\n- `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/anvil-voice extensions/voice-call/src/webhook/realtime-handler.ts extensions/voice-call/src/webhook/realtime-handler.test.ts` -> pass\n- `corepack pnpm plugins:inventory:check` -> pass\n- `corepack pnpm docs:check-mdx docs/providers/anvil-voice.md docs/plugins/voice-call.md docs/nodes/talk.md docs/web/control-ui.md docs/plugins/reference/anvil-voice.md` -> pass\n- `node scripts/check-extension-package-tsc-boundary.mjs --mode=compile` -> pass\n- `node scripts/check-extension-plugin-sdk-boundary.mjs --mode=plugin-sdk-internal extensions/anvil-voice` -> pass\n- `node scripts/check-extension-plugin-sdk-boundary.mjs --mode=relative-outside-package extensions/anvil-voice` -> pass\n- `node --check scripts/lib/changed-extensions.mjs && node --check scripts/lib/extension-test-plan.mjs` -> pass\n- `git diff --check` -> pass\n- fakoli-mini Mini validator with external lifecycle -> supported, no failure modes\n- fakoli-mini OpenClaw Gateway signed websocket smoke -> pass, transcript plus realtime audio response observed\n\n## Companion\n- Operator sync/evidence PR: https://github.com/fakoli/anvil-serving/pull/162\n\n## Note\nThe currently installed OpenClaw Gateway on fakoli-mini is 2026.6.11, so its catalog still reports `brains:[\"none\"]` for the live installed core. This PR changes source catalog behavior to `agent-consult`, and gateway tests cover the expected brain for gateway-relay realtime providers.",
        "branch": "codex/anvil-voice-openclaw-option",
